1379:Generated_Source\PSoC5/UART_DBG.c ****     /*******************************************************************************
1380:Generated_Source\PSoC5/UART_DBG.c ****     * Function Name: UART_DBG_SendBreak
1381:Generated_Source\PSoC5/UART_DBG.c ****     ********************************************************************************
1382:Generated_Source\PSoC5/UART_DBG.c ****     *
1383:Generated_Source\PSoC5/UART_DBG.c ****     * Summary:
1384:Generated_Source\PSoC5/UART_DBG.c ****     *  Transmits a break signal on the bus.
1385:Generated_Source\PSoC5/UART_DBG.c ****     *
1386:Generated_Source\PSoC5/UART_DBG.c ****     * Parameters:
1387:Generated_Source\PSoC5/UART_DBG.c ****     *  uint8 retMode:  Send Break return mode. See the following table for options.
1388:Generated_Source\PSoC5/UART_DBG.c ****     *   UART_DBG_SEND_BREAK - Initialize registers for break, send the Break
1389:Generated_Source\PSoC5/UART_DBG.c ****     *       signal and return immediately.
1390:Generated_Source\PSoC5/UART_DBG.c ****     *   UART_DBG_WAIT_FOR_COMPLETE_REINIT - Wait until break transmission is
1391:Generated_Source\PSoC5/UART_DBG.c ****     *       complete, reinitialize registers to normal transmission mode then return
1392:Generated_Source\PSoC5/UART_DBG.c ****     *   UART_DBG_REINIT - Reinitialize registers to normal transmission mode
1393:Generated_Source\PSoC5/UART_DBG.c ****     *       then return.
1394:Generated_Source\PSoC5/UART_DBG.c ****     *   UART_DBG_SEND_WAIT_REINIT - Performs both options: 
1395:Generated_Source\PSoC5/UART_DBG.c ****     *      UART_DBG_SEND_BREAK and UART_DBG_WAIT_FOR_COMPLETE_REINIT.
1396:Generated_Source\PSoC5/UART_DBG.c ****     *      This option is recommended for most cases.
1397:Generated_Source\PSoC5/UART_DBG.c ****     *
1398:Generated_Source\PSoC5/UART_DBG.c ****     * Return:
1399:Generated_Source\PSoC5/UART_DBG.c ****     *  None.
1400:Generated_Source\PSoC5/UART_DBG.c ****     *
1401:Generated_Source\PSoC5/UART_DBG.c ****     * Global Variables:
1402:Generated_Source\PSoC5/UART_DBG.c ****     *  UART_DBG_initVar - checked to identify that the component has been
1403:Generated_Source\PSoC5/UART_DBG.c ****     *     initialized.
1404:Generated_Source\PSoC5/UART_DBG.c ****     *  txPeriod - static variable, used for keeping TX period configuration.
1405:Generated_Source\PSoC5/UART_DBG.c ****     *
1406:Generated_Source\PSoC5/UART_DBG.c ****     * Reentrant:
1407:Generated_Source\PSoC5/UART_DBG.c ****     *  No.
1408:Generated_Source\PSoC5/UART_DBG.c ****     *
1409:Generated_Source\PSoC5/UART_DBG.c ****     * Theory:
1410:Generated_Source\PSoC5/UART_DBG.c ****     *  SendBreak function initializes registers to send 13-bit break signal. It is
1411:Generated_Source\PSoC5/UART_DBG.c ****     *  important to return the registers configuration to normal for continue 8-bit
1412:Generated_Source\PSoC5/UART_DBG.c ****     *  operation.
1413:Generated_Source\PSoC5/UART_DBG.c ****     *  There are 3 variants for this API usage:
1414:Generated_Source\PSoC5/UART_DBG.c ****     *  1) SendBreak(3) - function will send the Break signal and take care on the
1415:Generated_Source\PSoC5/UART_DBG.c ****     *     configuration returning. Function will block CPU until transmission
1416:Generated_Source\PSoC5/UART_DBG.c ****     *     complete.
1417:Generated_Source\PSoC5/UART_DBG.c ****     *  2) User may want to use blocking time if UART configured to the low speed
1418:Generated_Source\PSoC5/UART_DBG.c ****     *     operation
1419:Generated_Source\PSoC5/UART_DBG.c ****     *     Example for this case:
1420:Generated_Source\PSoC5/UART_DBG.c ****     *     SendBreak(0);     - initialize Break signal transmission
1421:Generated_Source\PSoC5/UART_DBG.c ****     *         Add your code here to use CPU time
1422:Generated_Source\PSoC5/UART_DBG.c ****     *     SendBreak(1);     - complete Break operation
1423:Generated_Source\PSoC5/UART_DBG.c ****     *  3) Same to 2) but user may want to initialize and use the interrupt to
1424:Generated_Source\PSoC5/UART_DBG.c ****     *     complete break operation.
1425:Generated_Source\PSoC5/UART_DBG.c ****     *     Example for this case:
1426:Generated_Source\PSoC5/UART_DBG.c ****     *     Initialize TX interrupt with "TX - On TX Complete" parameter
1427:Generated_Source\PSoC5/UART_DBG.c ****     *     SendBreak(0);     - initialize Break signal transmission
1428:Generated_Source\PSoC5/UART_DBG.c ****     *         Add your code here to use CPU time
1429:Generated_Source\PSoC5/UART_DBG.c ****     *     When interrupt appear with UART_DBG_TX_STS_COMPLETE status:
1430:Generated_Source\PSoC5/UART_DBG.c ****     *     SendBreak(2);     - complete Break operation
ARM GAS  C:\Users\Usuario\AppData\Local\Temp\ccNmiz7N.s 			page 50


1431:Generated_Source\PSoC5/UART_DBG.c ****     *
1432:Generated_Source\PSoC5/UART_DBG.c ****     * Side Effects:
1433:Generated_Source\PSoC5/UART_DBG.c ****     *  The UART_DBG_SendBreak() function initializes registers to send a
1434:Generated_Source\PSoC5/UART_DBG.c ****     *  break signal.
1435:Generated_Source\PSoC5/UART_DBG.c ****     *  Break signal length depends on the break signal bits configuration.
1436:Generated_Source\PSoC5/UART_DBG.c ****     *  The register configuration should be reinitialized before normal 8-bit
1437:Generated_Source\PSoC5/UART_DBG.c ****     *  communication can continue.
